{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A markdown doc describing a component's props is a separate copy of information the code already has, and it silently drifts the moment someone changes the component without updating the doc.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Storybook (or similar) renders the real component with controls generated from its real prop types — the docs can't describe a prop that no longer exists, because there's no longer a type to generate it from.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Require a story per exported component in CI and publish Storybook per-PR so a prop change's doc impact shows up in the same review, not as a deferred follow-up nobody circles back to.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
